# `std::collections::hash_map` — Open-Addressing Hash Table (`HashMap`)

## 1. Design Intent & Rust `hashbrown` / `std::collections::HashMap` Comparison

In Rust's `hashbrown::RawTable`, open-addressing bucket probing, tombstone management, and 75%/87.5% load-factor resizing rely on raw control bytes (`Bucket<T>`, `NonNull<u8>`) and `unsafe` pointer arithmetic.

In Jenny's `std::collections::hash_map`, `HashMap` stores flat `(state, key, val)` triples inside a single contiguous `std::mem::raw_buf::RawBuf` (`self.buf.cap == self.cap * 3`, requiring only 1 heap allocation per map) and enforces its load-factor and occupancy invariants at every method boundary:
- `invariant self.len * 4 <= self.cap * 3` (strict $\le 75\%$ load factor)
- `invariant self.len + self.tombstones <= self.cap`
- Automatic $2\times$ table growth and tombstone purging (`rehash_to`) when `(len + tombstones + 1) * 4 > cap * 3`
- Tombstone-reuse on `insert` and deterministic memory reclamation via `drop_map(mut self)`.

## 2. Formal Interface & Contracts

```jenny
module std_collections_hash_map

import std::mem::raw_buf

pub enum MapError {
    KeyNotFound,
    CapacityOverflow,
}

pub struct HashMap {
    buf: RawBuf,
    cap: i64 = 0,
    len: i64 = 0,
    tombstones: i64 = 0,

    invariant self.cap >= 0 && self.len >= 0 && self.tombstones >= 0
    invariant self.buf.cap == self.cap * 3
    invariant self.len + self.tombstones <= self.cap
    invariant self.len * 4 <= self.cap * 3
}

impl HashMap {
    pub fn new() -> HashMap
        effects []
        ensures result.len == 0 && result.cap == 0

    pub fn with_capacity(initial_cap: i64) -> HashMap ! MapError
        effects [AllocNative]
        requires initial_cap >= 0 && initial_cap <= 262144 else MapError.CapacityOverflow
        ensures result.len == 0 && result.cap == initial_cap

    pub fn len(self) -> i64
        effects []
        ensures result == self.len

    pub fn capacity(self) -> i64
        effects []
        ensures result == self.cap

    pub fn is_empty(self) -> bool
        effects []
        ensures result == (self.len == 0)

    pub fn rehash_to(mut self, new_cap: i64) -> i64 ! MapError
        effects [Mutate, AllocNative]
        requires new_cap >= 8 && new_cap <= 262144 else MapError.CapacityOverflow
        requires self.len * 4 <= new_cap * 3 else MapError.CapacityOverflow
        ensures self.cap == new_cap && self.len == old(self.len) && self.tombstones == 0

    pub fn insert(mut self, key: i64, val: i64) -> i64 ! MapError
        effects [Mutate, AllocNative]
        requires self.len < 196608 else MapError.CapacityOverflow
        ensures self.len >= old(self.len) && self.len <= old(self.len) + 1

    pub fn get(self, key: i64) -> i64 ! MapError
        effects []

    pub fn contains_key(self, key: i64) -> bool
        effects []

    pub fn remove(mut self, key: i64) -> i64 ! MapError
        effects [Mutate]
        requires self.len > 0 else MapError.KeyNotFound
        ensures self.len == old(self.len) - 1

    pub fn drop_map(mut self) -> i64
        effects [Mutate, AllocNative]
        ensures self.len == 0 && self.cap == 0 && self.buf.cap == 0
}

@example("EX-STD-MAP-01: HashMap open-addressing insert, 75% load-factor rehash, update, and tombstone remove") {
    var m = HashMap.new()
    assert(m.is_empty())
    var i = 1
    while i <= 10 {
        m.insert(i * 17, i * 100)!
        i += 1
    }
    assert(m.len() == 10)
    assert(m.capacity() == 16)
    assert(m.get(17)! == 100)
    assert(m.get(170)! == 1000)
    m.insert(51, 9999)!
    assert(m.len() == 10)
    assert(m.get(51)! == 9999)
    val removed = m.remove(51)!
    assert(removed == 9999)
    assert(m.len() == 9)
    assert(!m.contains_key(51))
    m.insert(51, 777)!
    assert(m.len() == 10)
    assert(m.get(51)! == 777)
    m.drop_map()
    assert(active_native_boxes() == 0)
}

@example("EX-STD-MAP-02: HashMap rejects missing key lookup and missing key removal") {
    var m = HashMap.with_capacity(8)!
    m.insert(42, 840)!
    val e1 = m.get(99)
    assert(e1 is Err(MapError.KeyNotFound))
    val e2 = m.remove(99)
    assert(e2 is Err(MapError.KeyNotFound))
    m.drop_map()
    assert(active_native_boxes() == 0)
}
```
